1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:04,340
Hey everyone, this is Day 1 of building in public.

2
00:00:04,290 --> 00:00:09,387
Today I'm going to show you a demo of my Koi Fish live wallpaper.

3
00:00:09,387 --> 00:00:11,935
And it's actually interactive.

4
00:00:11,935 --> 00:00:18,990
Just click anywhere on the water to drop some fish food, and watch the koi swim over to eat it.

5
00:00:18,990 --> 00:00:26,670
If the food lands on a lotus leaf, or a fish swims underneath one, the leaves move and react to it.

6
00:00:26,670 --> 00:00:35,937
You've got ripples on the water, tiny air bubbles, soft shadows from the lotus flowers, and a lot more little details like that.

7
00:00:35,937 --> 00:00:38,425
You can also customize it.

8
00:00:38,425 --> 00:00:52,055
Change how many fish are in the pond, set the frame rate anywhere from 20 all the way up to 144 FPS, and pick the render quality: low, medium, high, or ultra.

9
00:00:52,055 --> 00:00:59,663
Next, I'm thinking about adding a day and night cycle, so you can see how the pond looks after dark.

10
00:00:59,663 --> 00:01:03,557
And maybe a rainy day effect on the water too.

11
00:01:03,557 --> 00:01:10,072
And honestly, if anyone's interested in building this with me, send me a message.

12
00:01:10,072 --> 00:01:16,766
I'm looking for someone with a similar mindset to build things with and bounce ideas off.

13
00:01:16,766 --> 00:01:21,165
Building together is just way more fun than going solo.

14
00:01:21,165 --> 00:01:26,129
Things move faster, and constant discussion makes the app better.

15
00:01:26,129 --> 00:01:29,747
I've also worked on Android development.

16
00:01:29,747 --> 00:01:39,002
So if you'd like to build this, and sell it, together, drop a DM or a comment, and let's see if we can work together.

17
00:01:39,002 --> 00:01:41,730
Oh, and one last thing.

18
00:01:41,730 --> 00:01:45,709
How much would you be willing to pay for a wallpaper like this?

19
00:01:45,709 --> 00:01:48,197
Let me know in the comments.

